Disable the KIQ path for PASID TLB flushes on gfx1013.

Without this the KIQ fence times out, the CP ends up in an unrecoverable
state and the GPU reset fails to bring SDMA back:

  amdgpu: timeout waiting for kiq fence
  amdgpu: TLB flush failed for PASID 5
  amdgpu: The cp might be in an unrecoverable state due to an
          unsuccessful queues preemption
  amdgpu: GPU reset begin!
  amdgpu: [drm:amdgpu_ring_test_helper] *ERROR* ring sdma1 test failed (-110)
  amdgpu: resume of IP block <sdma_v5_0> failed -110

Verified by A/B on the same machine: stock module reproduces the above and
wedges the GPU; patched module runs a full Stable Diffusion pipeline with
zero errors. Reverting the patch reproduces the failure again.

Original patch by neoney (BC-250 community). Independently verified here.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -969,7 +969,7 @@ static int gmc_v10_0_hw_init(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block)
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = ip_block->adev;
 	int r;
 
-	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = !amdgpu_emu_mode;
+	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = false; /* gfx1013/BC-250: KIQ TLB flush wedges */
 
 	/* The sequence of these two function calls matters.*/
 	gmc_v10_0_init_golden_registers(adev);
